    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d813">

                <pb facs="1090" n="980" xml:id="pg980"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">367.1164 Brusa School Trial/48: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Turkey</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Grew</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-08-21T16:00:00+02:00"><hi rendition="#italic">August 21,
                                1928—4 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received August 22—6:32
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>100. My 89, July 3, 7 p.m.<anchor n="66" xml:id="d813-f1"/> Government has given
                    permission to reopen American school at Talas. I am furthermore advised
                    unofficially that American teachers at Brusa have won their appeal and will have
                    a new trial. This latter information should not be announced to the press until
                    officially confirmed.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
